# Everything, including the real build. A commit that only exists
# locally is your problem; a pushed one is everyone's.
#
# Repeats the pre-commit gates on purpose: commits arrive here from
# merges, rebases and --no-verify too, so this cannot assume they ran.
#
# `pnpm build` needs a complete .env - src/shared/config/env.server.ts
# validates it at boot and the build boots the app to prerender
# robots.txt and sitemap.xml. If this fails naming a variable, fill it
# in from .env.template; that is the check doing its job.
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint
pnpm format:check
pnpm test
pnpm build
